46edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","taskId":"container-recipe"},{"mergeCommit":"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f","revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"}],"checkpoints":[],"remaining":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package","cp-weights","cp-build","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close"],"frontier":["proxy-tooling"],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/7","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate \"conflict-domains\" because attempt 1 left the assigned lane at the prepared base with nothing to own: the worktree is clean, HEAD is still 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, the task diff is empty, and neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh nor any new file under tests/ exists on disk, so the accompanying 10 s finalMessage projection timeout is a downstream symptom of an attempt that ended without committing rather than an independent machinery fault. The whole remedy sits inside the authorized prefixes scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/, so attempt 2 should redo the work and land it. Steering for attempt 2: (1) Write scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh (bash shebang, set -euo pipefail, REPO_ROOT from dirname, IMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\", podman run with --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host and -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\", heredoc'd python payload) after reading specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md, and specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md. (2) BOUNDARY HAZARD — authorized-comment 7 instructs staging results/receipts/proxy.json, but results/ is NOT in this task's conflict domains; staging that path is exactly what the conflict-domains gate rejects on the next attempt. run-proxy.sh must still WRITE results/receipts/proxy.json at runtime (the acceptance argv greps the literal string 'results/receipts/proxy.json' out of the script), but the generated receipt must not be added to the commit. scripts/receipts-verify.py only validates the *.json files that happen to be present, so leaving proxy.json untracked keeps tests/test_repo_invariants.py green. Stage only scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and paths under tests/. (3) Carry the substantive fixes already established by steering: serve text-only with --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' to avoid the vision-encoder profiling allocation, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY=0 (superseded; integrated_gpu=False on this host), optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True, and record the flag choice in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. Serve with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, request one greedy completion, assert finite logits through the API, and shut down cleanly. (4) Reuse the fork's own tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout to synthesize the /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy checkpoint (same architecture identifier as the workload, a few layers, 8 block-FP8 experts with weight_block_size 128 by 128, small lookup table with the shard tensor name the mmap path expects) instead of writing a fresh generator; the existing /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy tree and the flashnext:dev image survive from prior attempts and should not be rebuilt if valid. (5) Terminal sequence, in order and without exception: run the acceptance argv `bash -euc \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"` and observe it pass; git add only the in-domain paths; git commit; then confirm `git status --porcelain` reports nothing before emitting the final message. An uncommitted worktree at exit reproduces this exact failure.","taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"retry"}],"retries":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/5","reason":"Stage `ownership` faulted.\n\nThe judge classified this failure as transient.\n\nAborted before the worker committed anything, so the ownership gate \"conflict-domains\" failed on an empty change set rather than on a boundary violation. Evidence: diff.head equals baseRev 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa with an empty patch; the lane worktree is clean (git status --porcelain empty, docs/ still holds only the pre-existing GATE0.md, CONTINGENCY patch, and .gitkeep), so no partial or uncommitted task work exists to preserve. The recorded cause is adapter-side: result-schema-mismatch wrapping result-projection-timeout, where the configured finalMessage capture for adapter \"spec-build-driver\" was not projected within 10000 ms and exitEvidencePassed was false; stderr \"spec-build-driver: agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\" is the downstream consequence of that lost session, not an independent implementation finding. Nothing in the record implicates the task definition: the goal writes only docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the binding conflictDomains prefix [\"docs\"], the single acceptance criterion ledger-sections is satisfiable entirely within that prefix, and both dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are already merged into the prepared base as commits b474021 and 71f2beb. There is no needs-authority envelope, no workerOutcomeClaim, no steering, and no prior diagnosis, so there is no substantive defect for attempt-2 steering to correct and no out-of-task authority or gate-contract change to propose. This is a harness or session fault that should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget: re-dispatch the same task revision sha256:4c0b640cab49ea7ac3b57b4e23f66c726b92fcce08e77d0f8816814181c3ba0a unchanged on the same lane so the driver can capture a final message and land a commit.","taskId":"morning-ledger"}],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[{"taskId":"cp-weights","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-build","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-smoke","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-proxy","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-tp2","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-bench","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-close","waitingOn":["rdma-package"]}],"blocked":[],"quiescent":false,"escalation":null,"closingSummary":null,"warnings":[]},"maintenance":{"blockingJobs":[],"cleaned":["pass:/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/.state/passes/72712d874766.json"],"currentRunHash":"102df659ef63","liveRuns":[],"warnings":[]},"checkpoints":[],"merged":[],"published":null,"failures":[{"taskId":"proxy-tooling","stage":"ownership","verdict":"failed","detail":"{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a04d14-8421-7443-8730-31bb6cc8d94f\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false}}}}"}],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":2,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/8","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.","id":"proxy-scripts-clean"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","git ls-files --error-unmatch scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh >/dev/null && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""],"description":"Both scripts are tracked at HEAD and the worktree is clean, which is the condition attempts 1 and 2 failed.","id":"proxy-scripts-committed"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qi 'enforce.eager\\|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"run-proxy.sh encodes the established serve doctrine so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it: PLE mmap on, eager execution, and text-only multimodal limits.","id":"proxy-serve-flags-recorded"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","git diff --name-only 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa..HEAD | grep -vE '^(scripts/make-proxy\\.sh|scripts/run-proxy\\.sh|tests/|results/receipts/proxy\\.json$)' | { ! grep -q .; }"],"description":"Every path touched by the task commits stays inside the amended boundary, including the receipt.","id":"proxy-no-out-of-domain-paths"}],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Re-issue the proxy-tooling work with results/receipts/proxy.json added to the write boundary and with a commit-first ordering that decouples authoring the scripts from exercising them on the GPU. Deliverable 1 (must land as a commit before any container or GPU work begins): scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh written in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh (bash shebang, set -euo pipefail, REPO_ROOT derived from dirname, IMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\", podman run with --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host and -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\", heredoc'd python payload), per specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4 and the cited evidence notes. make-proxy.sh runs inside the container and synthesizes a tiny checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's own tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout rather than inventing a generator, and it must not assume /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy already exists because it does not. run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1, eager execution, gpu_memory_utilization 0.6, and --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' (text-only mode, which is what avoids the 274877906944-byte vision-encoder profiling allocation), requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits through the API, shuts down cleanly, writes results/receipts/proxy.json, and records the text-only flag choice in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. Deliverable 2 (separate commit, after the first has landed): the receipt produced by an actual run, now inside the boundary. The worker must finish every attempt with a clean `git status --porcelain`.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/make-proxy.sh","scripts/run-proxy.sh","tests","results/receipts/proxy.json"]},"redacted":true,"retry":null,"taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"continuation":{"created":true,"dedupKey":"campaign-cont